  "checkpoints": {
    "description": "The §8.1 checkpoint commitment, byte for byte. `state` is the part of the registry §8.1 requires committed — the name tree, the active prices, the pending set and, since r16, the unreserved set — and `logHash` is an input, the §8.2 log hash at this height. `nameRoot`, `pricesRoot`, `pendingRoot`, `unreservedRoot` and `commitment` are derived. Two implementations that agree on every other file here and disagree on this one publish checkpoints that never match. These values are r17: a pending `U` entry (tag 0x09) commits a 20-byte recipient — 20 zero bytes for a release, the awardee's 20 for an award. An r16 implementation, which committed no recipient, reproduces every case without a pending `U` and diverges on every one that carries one.",
